partintro.section:
&reftitle.intro;
The Io\Poll\Event enum lists the conditions an Io\Poll\Context can watch for and report, together with two modifiers that change how they are reported.
A list of cases is passed to Io\Poll\Context::add, Io\Poll\Watcher::modify and Io\Poll\Watcher::modifyEvents, and returned by Io\Poll\Watcher::getWatchedEvents and Io\Poll\Watcher::getTriggeredEvents.

   &reftitle.examples;

    Level-triggered and edge-triggered reporting


<?php
use Io\Poll\Context;
use Io\Poll\Event;
use Time\Duration;

[$reader, $writer] = stream_socket_pair(STREAM_PF_UNIX, STREAM_SOCK_STREAM, STREAM_IPPROTO_IP);

$context = new Context();
$context->add(new StreamPollHandle($reader), [Event::Read, Event::EdgeTriggered]);

fwrite($writer, 'ping');
var_dump(count($context->wait(Duration::fromMilliseconds(10))));

// The data was not read, but the readiness is not reported a second time.
var_dump(count($context->wait(Duration::fromMilliseconds(10))));

fwrite($writer, 'pong');
var_dump(count($context->wait(Duration::fromMilliseconds(10))));


    &example.outputs.similar;


int(1)
int(0)
int(1)
